# Rust / Cargo
target/
**/target/
# Cargo.lock IS TRACKED. Dew is an application, not a library: the lockfile is
# what makes a build reproducible, and ignoring it undoes most of what pinning
# Aether by commit buys. The `rev` fixes Aether; the lockfile fixes everything
# Aether and Dew pull in behind it.

# Node / Web
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.env
.env.local

# IDE / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
Thumbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini

# rendered widget snapshots
*.png

# A MOD'S OWN ASSETS ARE NOT SNAPSHOTS, and the rule above cannot tell them
# apart. `--snapshot` output is a build artefact that lands anywhere; a file a mod
# SHIPS is source, and `mod://` resolves against the mod's directory, so it has to
# be in the clone or the mod draws a missing-image box for everyone but its author.
# Milestone 2 sprint 4 added the first one.
!mods/*/*.png


# pesde install output
roblox_packages/
luau_packages/
.pesde/

# Private working notes. NOT ignored by anything in this repository until now --
# only by a global gitignore on one machine, which is not a property the drafts
# can rely on. A fresh clone, a second machine, or a contributor would all have
# committed them. The directory is deliberately outside the repository's history.
.artifacts/

# Rendered gallery images. Generated by `cargo run --bin gallery-coverage --
# --render`, and regenerated on demand -- reviewed by eye, never committed.
gallery/renders/
